⚡️🇺🇸 As America’s 250th Birthday approaches, a volunteer group of Americans are doing a ‘Sea to Shining Sea’ relay run, where each person is running a segment of land from San Francisco, California all the way to Washington D.C in time for the festivities on July 4th.

June 14th, the first group of runners took off on the 3,016mi (4,853.78km) run from San Francisco, and as of currently, the runners carrying the flag are roughly 140mi (225.30km) from Kansas City, Missouri after having just hit the 1,683rd mile (2,708.52km), the group started with 20 days to do the run, and have 1,333mi (2,145.25km) left, with the average runner pacing at 8.7 miles per hour (14km/h).

